================================================================================
Snap: Sovereign Air-Gapped AI Workbench & Intelligence Routing System
================================================================================

Snap is an on-premises, air-gapped AI workbench and multi-model routing
platform built on top of llama.cpp. By leveraging modern quantized models
(GGUF) and speculative decoding, the system allows massive open-weight models
to run efficiently and generate responses significantly faster on organization
servers. It is engineered specifically for secure, industrial, and defence-grade
deployments where data confidentiality is absolute and no data may ever leave
the premises.

================================================================================
PRODUCT MISSION & BACKGROUND
================================================================================

Background & The Industry Dilemma:
Refineries, Public Sector Undertakings (PSUs), defence-linked manufacturing
units, and government offices generate substantial volumes of routine but
highly sensitive knowledge work:
- Formal approval notes and board presentations
- Engineering calculations and design reviews
- Source code for internal utilities and SCADA systems
- Review of scanned engineering drawings (P&IDs), inspection reports, and SOPs

None of this confidential work can be processed through public cloud AI
assistants (such as Claude, ChatGPT, or GitHub Copilot) because the underlying
data is classified and business-critical:
- Piping & Instrument Diagrams (P&IDs)
- Proprietary financials and tender/vendor negotiations
- Unreleased military/industrial designs
- Internal correspondence, audits, and strategic notes

Company policies strictly mandate that this data remain strictly on-premises.
As a result, organizations face an unacceptable compromise: either staff perform
these tedious tasks manually (sacrificing massive productivity gains), or
employees quietly leak confidential data into public cloud tools to get work done.

Open-weight reasoning and vision models have reached the capability threshold
needed to power a genuinely useful enterprise assistant. However, off-the-shelf
deployable solutions tailored for industrial, air-gapped environments simply do
not exist. Snap solves this problem.
